WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:11.540
Dagny, we met when you were 103 years old.

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.000
And we talked about your long life.

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.220
Please come closer.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.920
We met when you were 103, and we talked about your long life.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.740
And I was unsure if I would meet you again.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.960
Yes.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:28.360
But, imagine, you're sitting here now, and you're 106!

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.120
Yes. And I'm almost uninjured!

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.720
Almost uninjured!

00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.340
It was a close call this time ...

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.280
You were hit by a car last week.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:46.820
I was almost home, ten steps away ...

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:49.820
... in the pedestrian crossing ...

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:52.940
... on my way up to the sidewalk ...

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:59.580
... when a girl came with her car, and she was probably on her mobile phone ...

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.180
... probably telling someone that she was almost home.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:05.160
And she drove straight into me, and I flew ...

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.520
... first on top of one side of the car and then down again on the other.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:15.780
Were you ...

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:18.680
Did you break anything?

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:21.040
I only broke my pinky finger!

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:28.020
And then your arm ...

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:34.860
Yes. And then I've got some bruises on my forehead.

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.620
But what was it like going to the hospital?

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.300
You haven't spent a lot of time in the hospital.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.300
That's perfectly fine, you're like a princess there!

00:01:48.820 --> 00:01:50.820
Okay? What ..?

00:01:50.820 --> 00:01:52.600
The food could be a little better.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:55.120
What's the problem with the food?

00:01:55.200 --> 00:02:00.120
It gets transported long distances, so it's cold when it arrives!

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:05.480
And I've always imagined that warm food should be warm and cold food should be cold!

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:07.860
Not everything should be served cold.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:15.520
You don't find being at a hospital boring?

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:20.900
No, there's almost too much happening there, it should be more calm!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:31.040
They do tests and give medicines in the middle of the night, one can't sleep!

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:38.360
You're still living quite an active life.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.640
Not just as a blogger, but you've become a public person.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.440
Yes.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.280
Have you been able to ...

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:46.660
... follow through with your appointments?

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.220
You've been at the hospital and at the same time had a premiere of your documentary ...

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.760
I mean, you couldn't be a part of your premiere?

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:54.720
Yes, I went to the premiere!

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:59.020
But I didn't drink champagne because I was on medicine.

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:11.400
I'm thinking ... Since the last time I met you ...

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:14.120
... a lot has happened in your life.

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:19.160
Yes, for sure. It wasn't as much fun in the beginning, but it gets better towards the end!

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:24.740
I'm not really sure why they selected me.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.720
Or how they found me.

00:03:29.360 --> 00:03:31.520
But I was blogging.

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:37.600
There were almost no near-100-year-olds who were blogging, they thought I was really crazy!

00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:41.620
But ...

00:03:41.740 --> 00:03:45.580
But I write well, I actually do.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.500
Yes. And a lot of people follow your blog.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:51.480
Proper Swedish, which I learnt in school.

00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:55.640
You write much better Swedish than I do, I'll give you that!

00:03:55.800 --> 00:04:00.440
You shouldn't be embarrassed about that, you're not really Swedish.

00:04:08.280 --> 00:04:13.460
Jonas and I were talking about ...

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:18.100
... preparing for when you leave this earth.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:22.980
I don't want to think about death, it's the saddest thing in this world.

00:04:24.620 --> 00:04:29.280
I'll live for today and tomorrow, I know nothing about when I'll die.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:34.220
Didn't you think that you were about to die when your husband died?

00:04:34.220 --> 00:04:35.640
Yes.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:42.000
Yes, I thought that was so sad and miserable, and I felt sorry for both myself and the entire world.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:46.000
But when I didn't die, I was forced to start living!

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:51.960
You can't just walk around and whine, you have to get a grip of your existence!

00:04:52.060 --> 00:04:56.100
I was actually very wealthy, I had several millions.

00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:58.360
I gave it to a cancer fund.

00:05:04.420 --> 00:05:07.920
And I saved a little for the funeral.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:12.180
And I got an old computer, it was quite a blessing.

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:19.440
I'm thinking about, Dagny, that when you're born in 1912 ...

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.480
... you've been witness to women getting the right to vote.

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:23.560
Yes.

00:05:23.560 --> 00:05:27.980
But women weren't very appreciated before in the world.

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:32.820
They were supposed to take care of their husband, children and household. And then ...

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:37.080
... they were supposed to be content, and best case they would also get a little pocket money.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:40.380
May I say a little something?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.820
Because there you are ...

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:46.120
Your generation is the first generation of women who actually ...

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:47.540
... have been allowed to vote.

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:48.080
Yes!

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:51.700
And who have been able to educate themselves and to work.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:52.700
And that's fantastic!

00:05:52.700 --> 00:05:55.220
But the worst thing when I was a child, was that ...

00:05:55.220 --> 00:05:58.060
... education cost money.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:03.940
If I had been able to study after going to school, I would have become a professor, at least!

00:06:09.060 --> 00:06:13.780
My mother was born in 1926.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.220
And ...

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:19.060
They took her and her two sisters to the doctor ...

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.920
... who measured their heads and spoke a little to them, and ...

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.700
... talked to them about what they could become.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.340
And they could choose between school teacher ...

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:29.940
... secretary ...

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:32.240
... or nurse.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.160
And do you know what my mother did?

00:06:34.160 --> 00:06:34.980
No.

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.080
She agreed to be a school teacher.

00:06:38.220 --> 00:06:41.800
She went down to the institute in Göteborg.

00:06:42.360 --> 00:06:47.960
And she said: «I'm not a man nor a woman, I'm a school teacher!»

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:57.440
She left there, never came back, and said: «I need to be free».

00:06:57.440 --> 00:06:59.820
And when I listen to you ...

00:06:59.820 --> 00:07:04.000
I feel like you've arrived at this «I need to be free».

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.240
Yes.

00:07:05.600 --> 00:07:09.720
Awesome! Excuse me! I will now return.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:15.100
I'm rooting for you!

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.600
Before we finish, I just have to ask you ...

00:07:20.600 --> 00:07:23.760
What has the doctor said, how long do you have to wear the bandages?

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.260
For three weeks.

00:07:26.260 --> 00:07:27.760
Three weeks?

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.260
Yes.

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.580
Impractical.

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:32.400
Yes. It's unpleasant.

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.740
But it's a good defense weapon!

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.900
Dagny, thank you so much!

